description:
The user requested to add `v-model` functionality to the `TuiEditor.vue` component. This allows components using `TuiEditor` to bind a variable to its content for reading and writing. The provided solution modified the component to accept a `modelValue` prop and emit an `update:modelValue` event when the editor's content changes, thereby implementing the `v-model` behavior.

```vue /home/codx-junior/codx-junior/client/src/components/document/TuiEditor.vue
<script setup>
import '@snowdreamtech-ui/vue-tui-editor/dist/style.css'

import { Editor } from '@snowdreamtech/vue-tui-editor';
</script>
<template>
  <Editor :initialValue="modelValue" @update:modelValue="onUpdate" />
</template>
<script>
export default {
  props: {
    modelValue: {
      type: String,
      default: ''
    }
  },
  emits: ['update:modelValue'],
  methods: {
    onUpdate(value) {
      this.$emit('update:modelValue', value)
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

